m01 SURVIVED the first run. Its test sent only content types that FastAPI's body parsing already refuses: no Content-Type, text/plain and form bodies all get 422 without the check (probed with and without it). The check's own effect is to refuse +json subtypes (application/vnd.api+json, application/merge-patch+json), which FastAPI parses as JSON. Two cases were added for them. That strengthens the test and loosens nothing. m01 then ran again at the same head:

    m01 M1 JSON only: CAUGHT - 2 failed, 3 passed

The M1 record is corrected: the cross-site concern was already met by FastAPI's own parsing, and the check is defence in depth for +json.

