Why the tests that pass under m16 pass (chat.py at 06713f1, before phase B):
- `test_card_data_is_refused_before_the_trigger` (both files): with no trigger in that chat.py, card data is still
  refused, so it cannot fail there. It is caught by m21 (the card refusal disabled at the head): 2 failed.
- `test_chat_py_never_reaches_the_handoff_desk`: a static pin that holds on any chat.py with no handoff code. It is
  caught by m22 (a northwind_backend import added at the head), together with
  `test_sa06_endpoint.py::test_chat_never_reaches_the_handoff_desk`: 2 failed.
- The near-miss, does-not-match, product or negated mention, status and headers, over-length and empty tests: each
  pins behaviour that existed before phase B and must stay (a non-matching message still reaches the assistant,
  refusals unchanged). Passing at 06713f1 is their point.

Why the 10 that pass under m17 pass (tool_scopes.py at 06713f1): the earlier fragments, no shopper tool name holding
a fragment, `allowed_tools` returning no case tool, and that shopper agents exist. All are invariants that held
before this row, because no shopper agent had a case tool. The 4 that fail are the ones that need "case" in the
fragments.

m20 failed on its assertion (it is in Vitest's JSON report as failed), not only on the unhandled render error that v1
logged.

